# M29 R2.3 Container App definition (az containerapp create --yaml, rendered
# from this template by scripts/live-m29-deploy-app.sh via envsubst).
# Two containers, ONE image, role via args - the plan's host shape:
#   proxy        CredProx forwarder, the only ingress'd container (INTERNAL:
#                external=false - zero public listener; the battery reaches it
#                over the internal ingress FQDN from the credprox-m29-battery
#                job - see aca-job-r2.yaml.tmpl, G2)
#   counterparty the three verifiers (JWT assertion / HMAC / mTLS client-cert),
#                localhost-only (no ingress rules route to it)
# Config carries ONLY the vault URI + plain plumbing: no secret material in
# env or files anywhere (that is the test). Registry pull is IDENTITY-based,
# not credential-based: registries[].identity selects the kubelet UAI (holds
# AcrPull from the Bicep), which the deploy script ATTACHES via
# `az containerapp identity assign` - identity selection on a workload that
# does not have the identity attached is inert. Environment-level identity
# does NOT activate pull (live finding 2026-11-06: UNAUTHORIZED until the app
# itself selects the identity. docs: azure container-apps
# managed-identity-image-pull). Still no username/password anywhere:
# registries carries server + identity only.
# Substitutions: $REGISTRY $ENV_ID $UAI_CLIENT_ID $KUBELET_ID $VAULT_URI $CALLER_HASH $CA_B64 $DEPLOY_IMAGE_DIGEST
# RUNTIME IDENTITY BINDING: with 2 UAIs attached, unset binding dies at
# startup - ManagedIdentityCredential 400 "Unable to load the proper Managed
# Identity" in every runtime container (live finding 2026-11-06). There is NO
# containers[].identity schema field to fix that with: live GET schema probes
# at every api-version this RP serves (2024-08-02-preview, 2025-01-01,
# 2026-07-01) show no such key, and PATCHing one is rejected 400 "Unknown
# properties identity in ContainerAppContainer". The pin is carried in env as
# MANAGED_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID, but the ENVIRONMENT HINT ITSELF IS NOT THE
# MECHANISM INSIDE ACA: wire capture (loopback MIC stub + the ACA identity-proxy
# env contract, Azure.Identity 1.13.1) shows the SDK does NOT append that env
# hint to the identity-proxy request here (it is honored only on the IMDS path).
# samples/AzureContainerApps Program.cs RuntimeIdentity.Credential() reads the
# value and passes it as DefaultAzureCredentialOptions.ManagedIdentityClientId -
# only that form reaches the wire as &client_id=... Value = the RUNTIME UAI's
# CLIENT id (a public identifier, resolved live by the deploy script - never
# the kubelet UAI, which exists only to pull images via registries[].identity
# and holds no vault/data-plane role: the identity-plane split this milestone
# proves).
#   $CALLER_HASH vault secret CredProxTest--caller-key-hash ("sha256:<hex>") - the
#                caller registry stores ONLY the hash; the key VALUE stays a
#                vault secret the battery fetches (samples/AzureContainerApps
#                appsettings wiring: CredProx__Callers__battery__Keys__0__*)
#   $CA_B64      vault secret CredProxTest--mtls-ca-b64 (base64 PEM of the test CA)
#                - PUBLIC trust anchor: the entrypoint installs it into the
#                container trust store so the counterparty server cert chains;
#                no secret material travels this path (vault stays the only
#                secret channel - see the sample README honesty notes)
name: credprox-m29-app
# NO workload-level identity section - two live findings 2026-11-06: nested
# under properties the CLI silently ignored it (app read back None); at top
# level the --yaml path delivered identity.type without userAssignedIdentities
# and ARM rejected the whole request ("requires identities to be assigned").
# Both identities (runtime UAI + the kubelet pull identity selectable by
# registries[].identity) are ATTACHED by scripts/live-m29-deploy-app.sh via
# `az containerapp identity assign`, the documented path, before the final
# spec pass. registries[] below is tolerated by the RP while dangling.
properties:
  managedEnvironmentId: $ENV_ID
  configuration:
    registries:
      - server: $REGISTRY
        identity: $KUBELET_ID
    ingress:
      external: false
      targetPort: 8081
      allowInsecure: false
    secrets: []
  template:
    scale:
      minReplicas: 1
      maxReplicas: 1
    containers:
      - name: proxy
        image: $REGISTRY/credprox-m29:latest
        args: ["--mode", "proxy"]
        env:
          - name: MANAGED_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID
            value: "$UAI_CLIENT_ID"
          # BUILD STAMP: current digest of the :latest tag (resolved live by the
          # deploy script). Any new push changes this value -> the template
          # changes -> a new revision is forced and pulls the fresh image;
          # every process echoes it (Program.cs build witness line).
          - name: DEPLOY_IMAGE_DIGEST
            value: "$DEPLOY_IMAGE_DIGEST"
          - name: ASPNETCORE_URLS
            value: "http://+:8081"
          - name: KeyVault__Uri
            value: "$VAULT_URI"
          - name: CredProx__Callers__battery__Keys__0__KeyId
            value: "battery-key-1"
          - name: CredProx__Callers__battery__Keys__0__KeyHash
            value: "$CALLER_HASH"
          - name: CREDPROX_TEST_CA_PEM_B64
            value: "$CA_B64"
        resources:
          cpu: 0.5
          memory: 1.0Gi
      - name: counterparty
        image: $REGISTRY/credprox-m29:latest
        args: ["--mode", "counterparty"]
        env:
          # NO ASPNETCORE_URLS: the counterparty owns its ports in code
          # (Kestrel ListenAnyIP 8082 http + 8443 https with client certs) -
          # the https endpoint needs the client-cert options the URL channel
          # cannot carry, so in-code ownership of both endpoints is the only
          # consistent shape.
          - name: MANAGED_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID
            value: "$UAI_CLIENT_ID"
          - name: DEPLOY_IMAGE_DIGEST
            value: "$DEPLOY_IMAGE_DIGEST"
          - name: KeyVault__Uri
            value: "$VAULT_URI"
          # Ruling B (2026-11-06): 2-minute stub tokens for the live P10
          # rotation witness. The proxy re-mints only at the EXCHANGED-token refresh
          # (lifetime x RefreshFraction 0.8), so at the 59-min default a rotation is
          # never refused inside the witness window. Default 59 (offline/unset) is
          # unchanged in code; the report states this 2-minute stub explicitly.
          - name: CredProxTest__stub-token-minutes
            value: "2"
        resources:
          cpu: 0.25
          memory: 0.5Gi
